MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next addition because it would let me control a lamp through the Echo devices I already use.",
    "The longer HDMI cable serves a concrete connection need for my Blu-ray player and TV, while a single microSD card gives me spare storage I can use with my existing card reader."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks repeat a need my recent Fire TV Stick 4K Max bundle already covers, and the first-generation Echo Show 5 duplicates my newer display and stand.",
    "The wired earbuds do not serve a current need, and owning Alexa devices does not make an older Fire tablet useful to me. The two-pack of memory cards is relevant, but I only need one spare right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My recent Amazon device purchases seem to have been taken as interest in more Amazon devices, even when they repeat functions I already have.",
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched to loosely related gadgets without a clear purpose in my current setup."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter: having newer streaming and display devices makes older alternatives less appealing unless I have a separate need for them.",
    "I am interested in additions that make existing equipment more useful, and the amount matters too: one spare memory card fits my current need better than two."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my connected-home and computer interests, but often confused useful additions with devices that duplicate what I already have."
}
